  <body>
    <a class="skip-link" href="#main">Skip to main content</a>

    <main id="main" class="page" tabindex="-1">
      <header>
        <p class="eyebrow">Curious cat care</p>
        <h1>Cat FAQ</h1>
        <p class="intro">Quick answers to common questions about feline behavior, health, comfort, and everyday care.</p>
      </header>

      <section class="faq" aria-label="Frequently asked questions about cats">
        <div class="example">
          <h2 class="question">
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-purr">
              Why do cats purr?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="answer-purr" class="details">
            <p>Cats often purr when they feel relaxed, but purring can also be a self-soothing behavior when they are nervous, uncomfortable, or healing. Context matters: a loose body and slow blinking usually point to contentment.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2 class="question">
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-knead">
              Why do cats knead blankets or laps?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="answer-knead" class="details">
            <p>Kneading starts in kittenhood when nursing, and many adult cats keep doing it when they feel safe. It can also help them mark a cozy spot with scent glands in their paws.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2 class="question">
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-water">
              How much water should a cat drink?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="answer-water" class="details">
            <p>Water needs vary by size, diet, weather, and health. Cats that eat wet food may drink less from a bowl. Fresh water, multiple bowls, and fountains can encourage healthy hydration.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2 class="question">
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-scratch">
              Why do cats scratch furniture?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="answer-scratch" class="details">
            <p>Scratching stretches muscles, sheds old claw layers, and marks territory. Offer sturdy scratching posts near favorite furniture, and reward your cat when they use the post.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="example">
          <h2 class="question">
            <button type="button" aria-expanded="true" aria-controls="answer-indoor">
              Can indoor cats stay happy and active?
            </button>
          </h2>
          <div id="answer-indoor" class="details">
            <p>Yes. Indoor cats thrive with daily play, window views, climbing spaces, puzzle feeders, scratching surfaces, and predictable routines. Short interactive play sessions are especially helpful.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
    </main>

    <script>
      const disclosureButtons = document.querySelectorAll(".question button");

      disclosureButtons.forEach((button) => {
        const details = document.getElementById(button.getAttribute("aria-controls"));

        button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
        details.hidden = true;

        button.addEventListener("click", () => {
          const isExpanded = button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") === "true";
          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", String(!isExpanded));
          details.hidden = isExpanded;
        });

        button.addEventListener("keydown", (event) => {
          if (event.key !== "Escape" || button.getAttribute("aria-expanded") !== "true") {
            return;
          }

          button.setAttribute("aria-expanded", "false");
          details.hidden = true;
          button.focus();
        });
      });
    </script>
  </body>
</html>
